{[#]} 1. Re8# {Mayet’s Mate is acheckmate patternwhere a rook is placed
right next to the enemy king whilst supported by a distant bishop. The king is
further obstructed by his own pieces.This type of checkmate is similar to the
Opera Mate, but the attacking Rook occupies a corner of the board rather than
being in the middle. Therefore, the supporting Bishop is on the long diagonal
as well.Two classic references support this naming of Mayet's Mate. Checkmate!
by Koltanowski and Finkelstein, page 165 is the first.  Compare with Opera
mate and show the difference} *

